      "message": "First of all, this CL should have an associated bug ticket, and that should be referred to via a Bug: \u003cbug number\u003e line. Then we could have a discussion on that ticket, rather than here. Secondly, you need a subject prefix on the first line of the commit. Since this is not upstream it should probably be \"ANDROID:\"\n\nAnyway, I question whether this is useful and whether it actually works. Page reporting is destructive: Pages reported as free are *freed* by the host; Not swapped. And the only pages in the crashkernel region which I would expect to be resident are those which the crashkernel was actually loaded into, by microdroid manager. So I would expect this patch to simply discard the crashkernel.\n\nAm I wrong? :)",
